---
import { Code } from "astro:components";

import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import IconPresetTable from "../../components/docs/IconPresetTable.astro";
import MotionDemo from "../../components/MotionDemo";
import MotionTokenTable from "../../components/docs/MotionTokenTable.astro";
import ReducedMotionTable from "../../components/docs/ReducedMotionTable.astro";
import { codeTheme } from "../../components/code-theme";
import { retuneMotionExample } from "../../data/snippets";
import { reducedMotionSnippet } from "../../utils/motion";

const code = "mt-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm [&_pre]:p-4";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Motion | Buril UI"
  description="How Buril components move, the motion tokens, and what reduced motion keeps."
>
  <h1 class="font-display text-3xl">Motion</h1>
  <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-muted-foreground">
    Buril moves slowly enough to follow and settles softly: ink settles, the plate presses. It is
    plain CSS, with no animation library and nothing extra to install.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-display text-xl">At a glance</h2>
  <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
    <li>Presses and hover answer at once; state changes and entries take longer.</li>
    <li>Things that move end on a soft spring that passes its target by about 3% and settles.</li>
    <li>
      With reduced motion, nothing moves, resizes or rotates. Color and opacity fades stay, because
      they are not movement.
    </li>
    <li>Focus rings never animate: they appear at once, at full contrast.</li>
    <li>
      Every value is a token in <code>:root</code>, and every component also works without the
      theme.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-display text-xl">Try it</h2>
  <p class="mt-4">
    Flip the switch, check the box, press the button, and hover or Tab to the icon buttons and the
    card. Then turn on the simulation and do it again.
  </p>
  <div class="bg-paper-grid mt-4 border border-border p-6">
    <MotionDemo client:visible />
  </div>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-display text-xl">Personality</h2>
  <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
    <li>
      <strong>The plate presses.</strong> A click nudges a button 1px down, like a letterpress.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Ink settles.</strong> A check draws like a burin stroke, a radio dot spreads like a
      drop of ink, and positions end on a soft spring instead of a bounce.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Small distances.</strong> Things move a few pixels; opacity carries most of the
      change.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Once, then still.</strong> Gestures play once per hover or focus and never loop.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-display text-xl">Tokens</h2>
  <p class="mt-4">
    Durations and easings live in <code>:root</code> in the theme. They do not change with the color
    scheme.
  </p>
  <MotionTokenTable />

  <h3 class="mt-8 font-display text-lg">Change the timing</h3>
  <p class="mt-4">
    Each component writes its token with the same value as a fallback, such as
    <code data-wrap>duration-(--buril-duration-fast,200ms)</code>, so it moves the same without the
    theme. To retune every component at once, redefine the tokens after the theme:
  </p>
  <div class={code}>
    <Code code={retuneMotionExample} lang="css" theme={codeTheme} />
  </div>
  <p class="mt-4">
    The values apply to every installed component. Try them with reduced motion both on and off.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-display text-xl">Reduced motion</h2>
  <p class="mt-4">
    When someone turns on reduced motion in their system, each component drops its movement:
    everything that moves sits behind Tailwind's <code>motion-safe:</code> variant. Fades in color
    and opacity stay, so state changes are still easy to notice. The Spinner is the one component
    that swaps in a different picture.
  </p>
  <ReducedMotionTable />

  <h3 class="mt-8 font-display text-lg">A global rule for your app</h3>
  <p class="mt-4">
    Buril ships no global reduced-motion rule, because it would also stop the fades. If you want one
    for your own code, paste this into your CSS. It stops the fades too:
  </p>
  <div class={code}>
    <Code code={reducedMotionSnippet()} lang="css" theme={codeTheme} />
  </div>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-display text-xl">Icon gestures</h2>
  <p class="mt-4">
    The IconButton's <code>motion</code> prop gives the icon a gesture. It plays when the pointer
    arrives or keyboard focus lands on the button, and only when motion is allowed. Pick the preset
    that matches the icon:
  </p>
  <IconPresetTable />
  <p class="mt-4">
    The gestures are CSS keyframes that the{" "}
    <a href="/docs/components/icon-button" class="underline underline-offset-4">
      Icon Button
    </a>{" "}
    item adds to your CSS when you install it.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-display text-xl">Interactive card</h2>
  <p class="mt-4">
    A Card with <code>interactive</code> is one link stretched over the card. On hover, and while
    that link has keyboard focus, the card lifts 4.5px over the base duration and a shadow fades in
    over the fast one. The lift needs motion; the shadow fades in every mode. The link's own focus
    ring still shows where focus is. Static cards never move.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-display text-xl">How components move</h2>
  <p class="mt-4">The rules every component follows, and that a new one must follow too:</p>
  <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
    <li>
      Movement waits for <code>motion-safe:</code>; <code>motion-reduce:</code> is only for a
      different effect, such as the Spinner's dots.
    </li>
    <li>
      Transitions list their properties, such as{" "}
      <code data-wrap>transition-[color,background-color,border-color]</code>.{" "}
      <code>transition</code>, <code>transition-all</code> and <code>transition-colors</code> would
      also animate the focus outline.
    </li>
    <li>
      Only opacity, translate, scale and rotate move. Width, height, top and left never transition.
    </li>
    <li>Focus moves and state changes never wait for an animation to end.</li>
    <li>A test fails if a component's fallback value drifts from the theme.</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
